From 7d5901e440a979945525654392504c5510a801b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shravan Chippa <shravan.chippa@microchip.com>
Date: Mon, 18 May 2026 10:31:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] media: microchip-vcpp: Tune cam_m_sec for high fps
 usecases

Changing the V4L2 initialization delay from 100ms to 10ms
is a necessary adjustment for high-performance 60fps video
streaming, particularly when using DMA-BUF for zero-copy
sharing between V4L2 and the display system (like DRM/KMS)

Signed-off-by: Shravan Chippa <shravan.chippa@microchip.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/microchip/microchip-vcpp.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/microchip/microchip-vcpp.c b/drivers/media/platform/microchip/microchip-vcpp.c
index 65be698737cc..7c73caa0cfe0 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/microchip/microchip-vcpp.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/microchip/microchip-vcpp.c
@@ -88,7 +88,7 @@
 #define MCHP_VCPP_NUM_CTRLS			1
 
 /* Minimum wait time for camera to stabilize */
-#define MCHP_VCPP_DELAYED_CAM_M_SEC		100
+#define MCHP_VCPP_DELAYED_CAM_M_SEC		10
 
 #define MCHP_VCPP_POLL_TIMEOUT_U_SEC		500000
 #define MCHP_VCPP_POLL_SLEEP_U_SEC		10000
-- 
2.34.1

